Each skill gives the agent {{ spec.info.title }} context for authentication, database operations, file storage, realtime subscriptions, functions, and more. Cursor loads a skill when a task matches its description.

## Commands

Agent-executable commands for deploying from your editor:

- **deploy-site**: Deploy an {{ spec.info.title }} site with the {{ spec.info.title }} CLI. Covers init, push, non-interactive CI/CD mode, site management, variables, and logs.
- **deploy-function**: Deploy an {{ spec.info.title }} function with the {{ spec.info.title }} CLI. Covers init, push, non-interactive CI/CD mode, function management, executions, variables, and local development.

## Hosted MCP server

The plugin configures the hosted {{ spec.info.title }} MCP server at `https://mcp.appwrite.io/` under the name `{{ spec.info.title | caseLower }}`. It gives Cursor access to your {{ spec.info.title }} organizations and projects, and to the latest {{ spec.info.title }} documentation.

Cursor starts a browser-based OAuth flow when the server first connects. Sign in to {{ spec.info.title }} and approve access; no API key, project ID, endpoint, or other secret needs to be added to `.mcp.json`.

After authentication, try:

> Use {{ spec.info.title }} to show my workspace context and list my projects.

If the server does not connect, open **Customize**, turn the `{{ spec.info.title | caseLower }}` MCP server off and on again, and complete the sign-in prompt. Do the same when the OAuth session expires, and check Cursor's MCP output logs for connection errors.

